    "title": {
     "en": "Pizza parts"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1/2 of a pizza and 1/4 of the same pizza: which is bigger?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "numerator",
     "denominator",
     "compare",
     "add"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) A fraction has a top number (numerator) and a bottom number (denominator).\nThe denominator tells into how many equal parts the whole is divided. The numerator tells how many parts we take.\n1/2 is bigger than 1/4, because fewer equal parts means bigger parts.\nAdd fractions with the same denominator by adding the tops: 1/4 + 2/4 = 3/4."
    }
   },
